# GUI04 run A -- the vex_wheelv chain, with C:\WHEELT.NAP as the `#Z` autorun.
#
# No pointer choreography: the program is the running process, and every
# `wheel` line is a synthesised USB boot-mouse report fed to
# drivers::usb::hid::mouse_report -- the very function the real xHCI poll
# calls, with the very report layout a real wheel mouse sends.
#
#   wheel +1      byte 3 = +1, report length 4  -> wheel up   -> scancode 0x59
#   wheel -1      byte 3 = -1, report length 4  -> wheel down -> scancode 0x5a
#   wheel 127 3   byte 3 = 0x7f but length 3    -> a mouse WITHOUT a wheel:
#                                                  must produce NOTHING
#
# Ticks are hz_200 (200/s) relative to the injector arming on the first pump
# with a live EL0 process.
600  mark A_ARMED
800  wheel 1
900  wheel 1
1000 wheel -1
1100 wheel -1
1200 wheel -1
1300 wheel 127 3
1500 wheel 1
1600 wheel -1
1800 mark B_DONE
